🔴 1. “The file couldn’t open in Protected View”

Why this happens

Excel blocks files that are:

Downloaded from email / Teams / SharePoint

From network or unknown locations

Considered “unsafe”


When VBA tries:

Set evalWB = Workbooks.Open(path)

Excel may block it before VBA can open it, which causes the next errors.


---

🔴 2. “Process ended with error: File not found”

Why this happens

Usually caused by:

File was already moved (Completed / Invalid)

VBA still tries to open it

Or filename contains special characters

Or Protected View blocked it



---

🔴 3. “Bad file name or number”

Why this happens

Triggered by:

Workbooks.Open on a blocked file

file.Move after file is already moved

Invalid path or missing folder

Illegal filename characters



